# Local-only entry point (each teammate keeps their own to avoid merge conflicts)
.idea/
Makefile
# tests/ sources ARE tracked — `make test` is useless if the tests it runs only
# exist on one machine. Only the built binaries are ignored. Listing them by name
# drifted twice: tests/test_PostHandler was listed and does not exist here, and
# four suites that gained a main() were never added. Match on "has no .cpp
# extension" instead, so a new suite needs no edit here.
tests/test_*
!tests/test_*.cpp
tests/dump_config
# Scratch binaries built by hand at the repo root. rb_test (a 55 KB ELF) was
# committed once already; this stops the next one.
rb_test
a.out
claude_chat
latest_claude
.mcp.json
study/
# Outgoing teammate messages: local relay material, pasted by hand. Keeping them
# out of the repo is the point -- a stale message that still names a teammate's
# bug gets re-sent by accident.
msgs/
report_chat

# school-provided binaries and runtime output
/tester
/cgi_tester
# Uploaded files are runtime output and stay out of git -- but the DIRECTORY has
# to exist, because config/tester.conf writes there and PostHandler answers 500
# when upload_directory is missing (PostHandler.cpp:65). Ignoring the whole
# directory meant a fresh clone could not accept a single upload: MEASURED, POST
# /post_body returned 500 before uploads/.gitkeep was tracked and 200 after.
/uploads/*
!/uploads/.gitkeep
# (built unit-test binaries are covered by the tests/test_* rule above)

# A's local session bootstrap. Deliberately NOT committed: CLAUDE.local.md
# already shows what happens when a per-developer bootstrap becomes shared --
# it addresses Member B and misdirects everyone else who opens the repo.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

# private fixture tree for tests/test_FileUtils (removed by teardown, but an
# assert() abort skips teardown and would leave it behind)
tests/.fixtures_fileutils/

# Third-party tester tree + its CGI binary: 12 MB of test data, not ours.
EngineX/
YoupiBanane/cgi_tester

